  {
   "id": "reading-candlesticks",
   "title": "Reading candlesticks",
   "minutes": 2,
   "body": [
    "A **candlestick** shows four prices for one period: where it opened, the highest and lowest it traded, and where it closed. The thick body runs from open to close; the thin wicks reach the high and the low.",
    "A green body closed above its open; a red one closed below. A long wick means the price went far and came back.",
    "Parity's free sources publish one closing price a day, not the high and low. So our daily candles open at the previous close and only span the two closes. The Trade page says so under every chart."
   ],
