  {
   "id": "rsi",
   "title": "RSI: gains against losses",
   "minutes": 2,
   "body": [
    "The **relative strength index** compares the average gain on up days with the average loss on down days over the last 14 periods, and maps the result to a number from 0 to 100.",
    "Readings above 70 are often called overbought and below 30 oversold. That only says recent moves were one-sided. A market in a strong trend can stay above 70 for weeks.",
    "RSI uses Wilder's smoothing: each new average keeps 13/14 of the old one and adds 1/14 of the newest move."
   ],
   "terms": [
