  {
   "id": "macd",
   "title": "MACD: two averages and their gap",
   "minutes": 2,
   "body": [
    "**MACD** is the gap between a fast average (12 periods) and a slow average (26 periods) of the price. When the fast one is above the slow one, the gap is positive: the recent trend is up.",
    "A signal line, a 9-period average of MACD, is drawn with it, and the histogram shows MACD minus its signal. Crossings are popular signals, but they come late by design, because averages lag.",
    "Like every indicator, MACD is a summary of past prices. Test any rule built on it with costs and data it was not tuned on before trusting it."
   ],
