  {
   "id": "bollinger-bands",
   "title": "Moving averages and Bollinger bands",
   "minutes": 2,
   "body": [
    "A **moving average** is the average close of the last n bars. It smooths the noise so the direction is easier to see, and it always lags.",
    "**Bollinger bands** draw lines two standard deviations above and below a 20-bar average. They widen when prices swing more and narrow when markets are calm.",
    "A close outside the bands is unusual for that window, not a signal by itself. In a strong trend prices can ride along one band for a long time."
   ],
